1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator]
Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[squeaking]

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hunters.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
[Satotz] With no further ado,
the Hunter Exam will now begin.

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
I am Satotz, your Examiner
for the First Phase of the Exam.

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
It's my responsibility to lead you all
to the Second Phase.

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
The First Phase is already underway.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
HOPE x AND x AMBITION

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
[narrator] It's been two hours
since the Exam began,

19
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
and the applicants have traveled
more than 30 kilometers

20
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,000
from the starting line.

21
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
No one knows how far they'll have to go.

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Nevertheless,
they struggle to match the leader's pace.

23
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
It is a monotonous course
with no end in sight

24
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
and applicants have already started
to drop out.

25
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[panting]

26
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Nicholas]
Extrapolated from historical data,

27
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
it's safe to assume
this will be a 40-kilometer course.

28
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
And if my calculations are correct,
we should be nearing the end.

29
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
[pants loudly]

30
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
[Leorio]
What the hell was I thinking?

31
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
You've got to be a monster
to pass the Hunter Exam

32
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
and I'm surrounded by them.

33
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
-[yelling] Hey, wait up, kid.
-[Killua] Hm?

34
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
How about you show
a little respect for the Exam.

35
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:24,000
What do you mean?

36
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
I mean quit using a damn skateboard.
That's cheating.

37
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
-How's that?
-How?

38
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
This is an endurance test,
that's how.

39
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
-[Gon] No, it's not!
-Huh?

40
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
What are you babbling about now, Gon?

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
The examiner guy only said
we had to follow him.

42
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Hey, whose side are you on, anyway?

43
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
-[Killua] Hey, how old are you?
-Twelve years old.

44
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
[Killua] Same as me.

45
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
I think I'll run for a little while.

46
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Cool!
[laughs]

47
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
-My name's Killua.
-Hi, I'm Gon!

48
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
[Leorio] Damn kids!
You're not going to make a fool out of me.

49
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
[labored breathing]

50
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
[Nicholas]
Impossible. Simply impossible.

51
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
My calculations are never wrong.

52
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
What's happening?

53
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Am I actually going to fail?

54
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Me? Fail?

55
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
No, that's preposterous!

56
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
[yelling] I won't accept that.
I won't!

57
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[Nicolas, groaning, gasping for air]

58
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[Amori]
Hey, rookie!

59
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[laughs]

60
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Damn, you're a real mess.

61
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
I don't think I've ever seen anyone
run out of steam this early.

62
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
[Amori] Yeah, he's right.
You must really be pathetic.

63
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
[Umori] You think someone like you has got
what it takes to pass the Hunter Exam?

64
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[Imori]
Don't ever come back, loser.

65
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[crying out]

66
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
[screams]

67
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
[Tonpa]
Here.

68
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Thanks for your help.
Great job, guys.

69
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,000
He won't be recovering from that
anytime soon, I can promise you.

70
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
And I bet you he won't be applying
for the Exam again, either.

71
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
I've really got to hand it to you

72
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
you sure do love crushing rookies,
don't you, Tonpa.

73
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[Tonpa snickers]

74
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
It's the only reason I get out of bed
in the morning.

75
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
[music plays]

76
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
[Kurapika] It's been about four hours
since the First Phase began

77
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
and we've run at least 60 kilometers.

78
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
How much farther do we need to go?

79
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[panting heavily]

80
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[Leorio]
Rookies almost never pass a Hunter Exam.

81
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Just one every three years or so.

82
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
I'm just a regular guy.

83
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
I don't stand a chance.
What the hell was I thinking?

84
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Damn it.

85
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
-[briefcase thuds]
-[Gon grunts]

86
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[panting]

87
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Hey, forget about him.
You've got to keep moving.

88
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
[yelling]
Man, screw this!

89
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:17,000
I'm becoming a Hunter,
no matter what!

90
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Damn it all!

91
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[snickers]

92
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
-[grunts] Got it.
-[Killua gasps]

93
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
That was awesome!
[laughs]

94
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
[Killua]
Can I try that later?

95
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Gon] Sure, if I can try your skateboard.

96
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
[Satotz]
We've reached the 80-kilometer mark.

97
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Now, let's pick up the pace a bit,
shall we?

98
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[heavy panting]

99
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
-He can't be serious!
-He's insane.

100
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Look at him prance up those stairs,
like it's no big deal.

101
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
He's not even out of breath.

102
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[Geretta] If he doesn't ease up,

103
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
people are going to start dropping
like flies.

104
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Hey, I've got an idea. Let's race
to the finish, see who's faster.

105
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
[Gon] Sure, okay.
But the loser has to buy dinner.

106
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
[Killua]
Yeah, you're on.

107
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
[both] Ready, go!

108
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[grunting loudly]

109
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
[Kurapika]
Are you okay, Leorio?

110
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Great. I've never been better.

111
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:40,000
If I forget how stupid I look,
it's a whole lot easier to keep going.

112
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[yells]

113
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[Kurapika laughs]
I suppose I should probably follow suit.

114
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Leorio, I have a question for you.

115
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:57,000
What's up? First Phase too easy for you,
so you've got to make it harder?

116
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Save your breath, Kurapika.
You're going to need it.

117
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Why do you want to be a Hunter?
Is it really just about the money?

118
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
It can't be.

119
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
We haven't known each other very long,
but that's not like you.

120
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,000
I mean, sure, your attitude is terrible
and you aren't too bright, either.

121
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
[Leorio grumbles]

122
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,000
But I know,
shallowness isn't among your downfalls.

123
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:25,000
I've known many people whose only passion
in life was money.

124
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
And I can tell you're nothing like them.

125
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
[Leorio]
You've got it all figured out, don't you?

126
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
-The Scarlet Eyes.
-[Leorio] Huh?

127
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
That's why the Kurta Clan was targeted.

128
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Scarlet Eyes are a special trait
possessed only by the Kurta.

129
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
When our emotions are heightened,

130
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:55,000
the color of our eyes will change,
taking on a shade of scarlet.

131
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
In that state, the color of our eyes

132
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
is considered one of the seven most
beautiful colors in the world

133
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
and they command a hefty price
on the black market.

134
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[Leorio] So, that's why
the Phantom Troupe attacked you?

135
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Your eyes?

136
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
They plucked the eyes
from each of my brethren's corpses.

137
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Not a single one escaped desecration.

138
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Even now I can hear them,

139
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
the anguished screams
of their darkened eyes.

140
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
I swear on my life
that I will capture the Phantom Troupe.

141
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Once I do, I'll avenge my clan
by taking back their eyes.

142
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[Leorio] That's why you want to be
a Hunter?

143
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[Kurapika] That's right.

144
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
If I become a contract Hunter
with wealthy clientele,

145
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
I'll have access
to black market information.

146
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
But you'll have to be
the kind of Hunter you hate.

147
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
You think you'll be able to swallow
your pride when you need to?

148
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:54,000
The blow to my pride is nothing.
Not when compared to my clan's suffering.

149
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,000
[Leorio]
Well, sorry.

150
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,000
I don't have some big noble cause
like you do.

151
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
The only thing I'm after
is money.

152
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
That's not true.

153
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
-Of course it is.
-It's not.

154
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Be honest. Do you really believe that
money can buy everything? Tell the truth.

155
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Damn right, I do.

156
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
For the right price,
you can buy treasures,

157
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
dreams, hearts,
and even people's lives.

158
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Take that back, Leorio.

159
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
I will not stand here
and allow you to insult the Kurta.

160
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Why?
It's the truth, isn't it.

161
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
If I had money,
my friend would still be alive today!

162
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Was he ill?

163
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Yeah. It was a curable disease.

164
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
The problem was that the operation
cost a fortune.

165
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
I was naive.

166
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
I figured I could become a doctor

167
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
so I could cure kids
with the same disease.

168
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
And tell their parents
they owed me nothing.

169
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
It was free of charge.

170
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
That was my dream.

171
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
A pretty good joke, right?

172
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Turns out, to become a doctor

173
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
you already have to have
an obscene amount of money.

174
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Get it now?
The whole world runs on money.

175
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
So I'm going to get
as much as I can.

176
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
See you at the finish line.

177
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Catch you later, old man.

178
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Hey, I'm not old.

179
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Can't you tell I'm a teenager
just like you?

180
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[Gon]
Huh? No way!

181
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:59,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

182
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:03,000
KILLUA

183
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[panting]

184
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
I can't go on.

185
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
This... this is it,
I'm finished.

186
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
[panting]

187
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
I've got to tell you, Gon.

188
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
I'm pretty impressed
that you can keep up with me.

189
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
You are?
[laughs]

190
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Or maybe they're all so slow,
you just seem fast.

191
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Man, I thought the Hunter Exam
was going to be more of a challenge.

192
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
This is boring.

193
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[Gon] Hey, why do you want to be
a Hunter, anyway?

194
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Who me?

195
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
-I never said I wanted to be a Hunter.
-Huh?

196
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
I just heard that the Exam
was supposed to be really hard.

197
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
It sounded kind of fun
so here I am.

198
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
But it's not as fun as I thought.

199
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
[Killua]
What about you?

200
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[Gon] Well, the thing is,
my dad's a Hunter.

201
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:59,000
So, I decided I was going to be
a Hunter just like him, no matter what.

202
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
[Killua]
Hm, so what kind of Hunter is he?

203
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
[Gon] No idea.

204
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
[laughs]

205
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
-It's the weirdest thing I've ever heard.
-Huh?

206
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
You wanna be the same kind of Hunter
as your dad

207
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
but you don't know anything
about him? That's nuts.

208
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Mito's the one who raised me.

209
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,000
and she told me a little,

210
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
but I've only ever seen him in pictures
she showed me from a long time ago.

211
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
-Wait, so who's Mito?
-She's my aunt.

212
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
She said that my dad took the Hunter Exam
when he was only 12 years old, too.

213
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
He passed his first try
and became a Hunter.

214
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
That's when he decided
to leave the island.

215
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,000
So, I came here in order to find out
why he chose being a Hunter

216
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
over staying at home with me.

217
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
[man]
The exit! Oh, thank goodness.

218
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
[man two] We're finally getting out
of this dark tunnel.

219
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Now then. Let's see how many applicants
have made it this far.

220
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
[both] Goal!

221
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[laughing]

222
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Yeah, I did it!
I finished first.

223
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:09,000
What are you talking about?
I totally won.

224
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
-[Gon] No, I won.
-[Killua] I won.

225
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
[Gon] I was faster than you,
so you have to buy me dinner.

226
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[Killua] No way.
I was faster so you're buying me dinner.

227
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[Gon]
Na-ah, I was faster.

228
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Hey, which one of us was fastest?

229
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
You crossed the finish line
simultaneously.

230
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Okay.

231
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Fine, I guess I'll have to buy
your dinner.

232
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:30,000
[Killua]
Huh?

233
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
But then you have to buy me
my dinner, okay?

234
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
I don't get it.

235
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Hey, Mr. Satotz,
is this where the Second Phase begins?

236
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
No, it isn't.
We have quite a way to go.

237
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
[Gon] Oh, man!

238
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[heavy breathing]

239
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[Leorio groans, laughs]

240
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[Gon] Hey, Kurapika!

241
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Hey.

242
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Is this our destination?

243
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Nope, not yet.

244
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Hm, I see.

245
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
-Looks like the fog is lifting.
-Ah, really?

246
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Whoa!

247
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[Satotz] The Milsy Wetlands,
also known as Swindler's Swamp.

248
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
We must cross it to reach
Phase Two of the Exam.

249
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
This place is home to
a variety of truly bizarre animals,

250
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:51,000
many of which are
crafty, voracious creatures

251
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
who deceive and feast
on human prey.

252
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
So please, be very careful.

253
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
If you're deceived,
you'll surely die.

254
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
[clamoring]

255
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
[creaking]

256
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
[grunting]
[yells] Wait for me!

257
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
These wetland creatures
are not to be underestimated,

258
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
for they will use every trick in the book
to fool their prey.

259
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,000
[gasping]

260
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,000
This is an ecosystem

261
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
in which all creatures hunt
by the art of deception.

262
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:32,000
And that is why it's also known
as Swindler's Swamp.

263
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Now then, please follow me closely
so you won't be deceived.

264
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
[scoffs]
Is he messing with us?

265
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,000
If we know they'll try to deceive us,
who's gonna fall for it?

266
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[man]
Don't fall for it!

267
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Listen, didn't I just say
that we won't?

268
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,000
[groans]
Don't let them fool you!

269
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,000
[surprised gasping]

270
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
He's lying.
That man is lying to you.

271
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,000
He's an impostor!
A total fraud.

272
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
I'm the real Examiner,
you got it?

273
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Impostor? What's going on here?

274
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
But then, who is he, really?

275
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
I'll prove it, look at this!

276
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,000
[clamoring]

277
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Oh wow, he looks like Mr. Satotz!

278
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
This is a man-faced ape
from the Milsy Wetlands.

279
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
A man-faced what?

280
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
The man-faced ape loves the taste
of human flesh.

281
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
But their limbs are really long
and thin, so they're actually quite weak.

282
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,000
That's why they disguise themselves
as humans.

283
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
They trick us into following them
into the wetlands,

284
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
where they work together with other
creatures to kill and eat us.

285
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:49,000
That's what he wants. To deceive
the entire Hunter applicant pool

286
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
and feast on every one of you.

287
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Bastard.

288
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Oh yeah?

289
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Well, then that would certainly explain
why he doesn't walk like a normal human.

290
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
What?

291
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
-[cards flutter]
-[everyone gasps]

292
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
[laughs]

293
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
I see, I see.

294
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
That settles it, then.

295
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
So you are the real one.

296
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[music plays]

297
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,000
[Hanzo] Hold on, he's the real Examiner?

298
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
[screeching]

299
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
The Examiners are Hunters.

300
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Each is hand-picked by the Exam Committee
to do this job without pay.

301
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Anyone who holds the title
we're vying for ourselves

302
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:53,000
could have deflected that attack.
And quite easily, I might add.

303
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
I shall take that as a compliment.
Thank you.

304
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Still, should you choose to attack me
again, for any reason,

305
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
I will have no choice but to report you
for attacking an Examiner,

306
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
and have you immediately disqualified.

307
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
-Is that clear?
-Of course.

308
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
[cawing]

309
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Nature can be so brutal.
It's hard to watch.

310
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
So he was a man-faced ape as well.

311
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
He was trying to confuse the applicants
and lure some of you away.

312
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
These attempts are to be expected.

313
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
-We can't let our guard down.
-Right.

314
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Please be aware
that you will encounter such deceptions

315
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,000
on a regular basis.

316
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
I must assume that
a number of you were fooled

317
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
into suspecting my true identity

318
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Oh, well, I uh...

319
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
[chuckles, embarrassed]

320
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Understand,

321
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:54,000
I want to make it abundantly clear
that if any of you are to lose sight of me

322
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
once we enter the fog
of the Milsy Wetlands,

323
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:00,000
you have no hope whatsoever
of reaching the Second Phase of the Exam.

324
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:01,000
You've been warned.

325
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Now, let's begin.
Please follow me.

326
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Oh, great.
It's another marathon.

327
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
Except this time
we're in a swamp

328
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:35,000
and running on wet ground requires
significantly more energy.

329
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
[narrator] The applicants have finally
left the long, dark tunnel

330
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
and stepped into the light.

331
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:45,000
So far, 36 candidates have
withdrawn from the Exam,

332
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
and 368 remain.

333
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Their next challenge will be
the Milsy Wetlands,

334
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
which is also known as
Swindler's Swamp.

335
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,000
The excruciating Hunter Exam
continues.

336
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Gon] Next time.
"Hisoka x Is x Sneaky."

337
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Okie-dokie!
